# slimcity

Quality-Diversity (CMA-ME) over headless Micropolis (SimCity 1). See README.md, RESULTS.md, EXPERIMENTS.md.

## Environment

- System Python 3.9; SWIG extension at `engine/build/_micropolisengine.cpython-39-darwin.so`.
- Build if missing: `cd engine && make swig && python3 setup.py build_ext --inplace --build-temp build/temp --build-lib build`
- Deps: `numpy`, `ribs`, `Pillow` (user install is fine).

## Experiments

- Save archives under `results/` with unique names (e.g. `results/exp_2026-06-03_cursor.npz`) — another machine/instance may be training in parallel.
- Append a row to EXPERIMENTS.md when starting a long run (config, wall time, insight).
- Archives embed full config in `.npz` metadata; replay with `record.py` / `plot_archive.py`.
- Do not commit `*.npz`, `*.gif`, or engine build artifacts.

## Code map

- `qd_train.py` — CMA-ME loop; `evaluate.py` — rollout; `policy.py` — ConvPolicy; `slimcity.py` — engine wrapper.
- Fitness: delta `cityPop`. Descriptors: `road_frac`, `ind_share`. Default map: empty (not preset cities).
- Prefer `record.py` over `viewer.py` on macOS (Tk is unreliable).
